course: dictionary
lesson: 9250
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word sort has more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one to use. A sort is a kind or type of something: «The shop had all sorts of animals for sale.» Here sorts means kinds, not a group of things being put in order.
explain: To sort is a verb, and it means to put things into groups by what they are like, or into an order. «Sort the cards by colour.» The clue is the cards: you group them. In maths you might sort numbers from smallest to largest.
explain: Sort out means to fix a problem or tidy something up. «It took a long talk with her mum to sort it out.» The problem was that the girl was unhappy, and sorting it out meant solving it. Sort of, in an informal way, means a little: «I'm sort of tired.»
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning. In «What sort of bird is that?», if sort means kind, then «What kind of bird is that?» still makes sense.
fact: Sort (noun) means a kind or type. «All sorts of» means many different kinds.
fact: Sort (verb) means to put things into groups or into an order, as in «sort by size».
fact: Sort out means to fix a problem: «sort it out».
fact: Sort of (informal) means a little, or in some way.
fact: In a Venn or Carroll diagram, sorting puts objects into groups by a property such as colour, shape, or even and odd numbers.
exercise: «The shop had all sorts of toys on the shelves.» What does sorts mean here? | *Kinds or types | Pieces of wood | Very large boxes | Tidied away at night
exercise: «Please sort these pencils by colour.» What does sort mean? | *Put into groups | Paint | Throw away | Measure
exercise: «Can you sort out the mess in your bedroom?» What does sort out mean? | Make it bigger | *Fix a problem or tidy something up | Leave it for later | Paint over it
test: «I'm sort of tired after the match.» What does sort of mean here? | *A little, in some way | Sorted into piles | Very, very angry | Asleep
test: Mrs Ali says, «Sort the numbers from smallest to largest.» What does sort mean? | *Put into an order | Count them out loud | Cover them up | Add them together
exam: In «An airport is like a huge machine for sorting people, bags and planes», what does sorting mean? | *Putting them into groups or order | Asking them questions | Flying them somewhere | Shouting their names
